course: dictionary
lesson: 15609
title: Tardiness: being late
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tardiness is a formal word for being late. You will often meet it at school, at work and at meetings. «Her tardiness made the whole class start without her.» The class started without her because she arrived late, so tardiness means lateness.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like school, bell, slip and late show the topic. «The school sent a note home because Sam's tardiness had happened three times this week.» Sam was late three times, so the note was about being late.
explain: Tardiness can also mean being slow to do something, not only being late for a place. «His tardiness in replying to emails annoyed his boss.» He was slow to reply, so the word fits here too. Check the sentence to see which meaning the writer means.
fact: Tardiness means being late, especially arriving late to school, work or a meeting.
fact: Tardiness can also mean being slow to do something.
fact: In the USA and Canada, schools often use «tardy slips» for students who arrive late.
fact: A «tardiness policy» is a school rule about what happens when you arrive late.
exercise: «Her tardiness made the whole class start without her.» What does tardiness mean here? | Being hungry | Being clever | *Being late | Being very happy
exercise: Ms Patel says, «Tardiness is not allowed after the bell.» What is she talking about? | Losing a pencil | Eating lunch too fast | *Arriving late | Drawing a picture
exercise: «His tardiness in replying made us wait a whole week.» What does tardiness suggest here? | Being quick and eager | *Being slow to do something | Being loud and noisy | Being sad about the news
test: «Sam's tardiness meant he missed the start of the spelling test.» What does tardiness mean? | Being sick at home | *Being late | Being very tired | Being rude to the teacher
test: A school may have a «tardiness policy». What is a tardiness policy about? | Rules about homework | Rules about sports kit | *Rules about arriving late | Rules about lunch and snacks
exam: «Your written excuse for tardiness must be signed by a parent.» What does tardiness mean in this sentence? | Being cold and wet | Being rude to a friend | Being noisy in class | *Being late
